{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>ואתמול</b> — one word, as in <b>כי ערוך מאתמול תפתה</b>. And the meaning: for my words bring good, not as it was yesterday." "<b>לאויב יקומם</b> — my people rise up as an enemy, a man against his fellow." "<b>ממול שלמה</b> — for the sake of a garment of splendor that they strip off, the outer garment of those who pass by trustingly. And when they escape being killed, so that nothing remains to them except what is on them, they reckon themselves as captives of war and rejoice in escaping from your hand, just as captives of war rejoice in peace. Thus you do outside the city to despoil spoil and to plunder plunder, and in the city you do other violence."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "The reading 'captives of war' (שבי) for people who escape alive follows the Hebrew as given; the logic is compressed and somewhat obscure but the translation is literal."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:45.572216917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}